    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1048">

                <pb facs="1528" n="1512" sameAs="frus:frus1949v06/pg1512"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867N.01/11–2949: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Jerusalem</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Roberts</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jerusalem</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1949-11-29T16:00:00+02:00">November 29,
                            1949—4 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>666. French Consul General Neuville today intimated King Abdullah and Ben-Gurion
                    holding secret meetings either in Jerusalem area or in South but actual location
                    talks unknown. General Riley discounts meetings on basis King’s statement that
                    although ready to treat would wait outcome of UN Assembly.</p>
                <p>Same source inferred Arabs and Jews negotiating exchange of Mt. Scopus and Sheik
                    Jarrah quarter for Arab quarters in South Jerusalem. Riley believes this report
                    may stem from his account of recent conversations with King.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 666; repeated Tel Aviv 136; Department pass Amman 79, Istanbul
                    unnumbered.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Roberts</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
